+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_title">🐢 What\'s New in TurtleLauncher</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_version">v3.1</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_feature_1">🎭 Emotes: dependencies install themselves</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_feature_1_desc">Installing the Emotecraft mod now automatically fetches its required Player Animation Library dependency (read straight from the mod\'s own metadata), so the game no longer crashes on launch with a missing-dependency error.</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_feature_2">📜 Game logs are finally saved</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_feature_2_desc">The game\'s own output — mod loaders, console messages, crash traces — is captured into the launcher log. The home screen\'s Last Game Log card shows the last session across restarts, and the Assistant can read it when you ask why the game crashed.</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_feature_3">📤 Share logs straight into the Assistant</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_feature_3_desc">Turtle Launcher now appears in Android\'s share menu. Share any game log (file or text) from any app and the Assistant analyzes it on the spot — no copy-paste.</string>
+    <string name="turtle_whats_new_warning">🧩 Renderer plugin apps (e.g. MobileGlues) show up in the renderer list right after you install them — no restart needed — and their supported Minecraft version range is honored like any built-in renderer.</string>
